      "nets": [],
      "observed": "ADS1115 U33 pin 1 (ADDR) has no net connection and is not marked no-connect.",
      "expected": "The ADS1115 address pin should be tied to a valid address-select level or signal so the device has a defined I2C address.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(pin (num \"1\") (name \"ADDR\") (type \"input\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U33\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"VDD\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "With ADDR floating, the ADC's I2C address may be undefined, potentially preventing reliable communication with U33 and its voltage measurement.",
      "confidence": 0.91
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R36"],
      "pins": ["R36.1", "R36.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTN", "VOUTP"],
      "observed": "R36 is specified as 24k in the netlist, but its MPN FRC0805J240TSD and description specify 24Ω. It is connected directly across VOUTP and VOUTN.",
      "expected": "The schematic value and the sourcing part must agree. If the intended value is 24k, as the netlist states, the specified MPN should identify a 24k resistor rather than a 24Ω resistor.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R36\") (value \"24k\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(field (name \"Description\") \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"219\") (name \"VOUTN\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"220\") (name \"VOUTP\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the BOM is sourced by MPN, a 24Ω resistor could be fitted across VOUTP and VOUTN instead of 24k, heavily loading the output and potentially overheating or damaging R36 or the supply.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The files show an unconnected ADS1115 address input and a clear mismatch between R36's schematic value and its sourcing metadata. Either can make the assembled board behave differently from the schematic's apparent intent."
}

